window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-074", "name_zh": "出体", "name_en": "out-of-body", "tagline": "意识离开肉体，到一个只稍微没那么具体的身体里走一趟——赛斯说这件事你每晚睡觉都在做，只是没带着醒着的记忆回来。", "explanation": "赛斯把出体讲成一件有身体构造做基础的日常事：人的生物机制本来就允许意识的一部分离开肉体再回来，每个人每晚睡着以后都会出去一段时间，只是醒着的意识没有跟着走，所以回来后被当成一个梦故事。出体时你并不是变成没有形状的东西，而是在一个只比肉体稍微不那么具体的身体里活动，两者之间还有一条由化学能量造成的电磁连结——这也是出体和死亡的区别：走开太久联系会断，出体的联系仍然在，所以一定会回来。赛斯同时提醒，那里的经验会跟着你的期望走，相信会遇见魔鬼的人就会遇见自己造的心念形相，所以想练的人得先知道自己在做什么；他的做法却异常日常：半夜醒来时试试在肉体留在床上时走进另一个房间，平时练习把醒时的意识带进睡眠。他说这份亲历的证据没有别的取法，却也不提供一套复杂方法——真正要改的是你探索人生的整个方式。", "definitions": [{"zh": "就那件事而论，肉体天生就善处理「意识的投射」（projection of consciousness）或魂游体外（out-of -body t ravel），不论你们喜欢怎么称呼它。你生物性的构造，包括了能容许你意识的某部分离开你的身体又回来的机制。", "en": "For that matter, the body is naturally well-equipped to handle “projection of consciousness,” or out-of-body travel, whatever you prefer to call it. Your biological makeup includes mechanisms that allow a certain portion of your consciousness to leave your body and return.", "source": "Session 758"}, {"zh": "当你在任意一种“出体”经验里离开了你的肉体时，你实际上是在一个较它只稍微不那么具体的身体里离开它。", "en": "When you leave your physical body in any kind of out-of-body experience, you actually leave it in another that is only slightly less physical.", "source": "Session 571"}, {"zh": "当意识离开了身体，走开了有好一段时间，那么联系当然就断了。在“出体”的情况联系仍然在。", "en": "When consciousness leaves the body and is away for some time then the connection is, of course, broken. In out-of-body states the connection still holds.", "source": "Session 537"}, {"zh": "当你有出体经验时，你可能开始更加直接觉知内在实相的本质。", "en": "When you have out-of-body experiences, you can become aware of the nature of inner reality more directly.", "source": "Session 304"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "出体不是特异功能：你每晚都在做", "note": "赛斯先拆掉「这是少数人才有的本事」这个前提。他说肉体天生就善处理意识的投射，人的生物构造里本来就带着这套机制，让它的一部分意识离开身体再回来，而且这些机制也是动物天性的一部分。接着他把范围推到极致：每一个人在每晚睡眠中都会离开身体一会儿，本能地出去不同长短的时间；那些旅程不是被安排好的观光滑线，你其实在自己规划自己的观光，可以一个人走，也可以和同伴一起。最反直觉的一条是：你出了身体照样做梦，所以这段经历常常被回来后的脑子包装成一个梦故事，肉体形象则继续在床上沉睡。至于为什么一辈子没几次有意识的出体，赛斯给的理由很朴素——只因为大多数人都相信自己不可能离开身体，这个信念本身就是那道闸门；而这类经验本来比文字更能让人了解将遭遇的情况。", "src": "第 758、537、536、719、710 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 758 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 537 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 536 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 719 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 710 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0119", "zh": "就那件事而论，肉体天生就善处理「意识的投射」（projection of consciousness）或魂游体外（out-of -body t ravel），不论你们喜欢怎么称呼它。你生物性的构造，包括了能容许你意识的某部分离开你的身体又回来的机制。这些机制也是动物天性的一部分。肉体配备好了可以许多其它中的经验，那是不被承认为天赋的人类经验的（The body is equipped to perceive many other kinds of experiences that are not officially recognized as native to human experience.）。那么，到某个程度，你学会经常地监控你的行为，以使它顺应为健全或理性的经验已建立好的评定行准则。", "en": "For that matter, the body is naturally well-equipped to handle “projection of consciousness,” or out-of-body travel, whatever you prefer to call it. Your biological makeup includes mechanisms that allow a certain portion of your consciousness to leave your body and return. These mechanisms are a part of the nature of animals as well. The body is equipped to perceive many other kinds of experiences that are not officially recognized as native to human experience. To one extent or another, then, you learn to constantly monitor your behavior, so that it conforms to the established criteria set up for sane or rational experience.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第758节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "758", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0064", "zh": "那么，所有这些情况按照所涉及的人而可能发生，或可能不发生。可是，在离开肉体之后，你将立刻发现自己在另一个“身体”里。这是与在“出体”时你用以旅游的同样的形体，让我再一次提醒我的读者，他们每一个人在每晚睡眠中都会离开身体一会儿。", "en": "All of these circumstances then may or may not occur according to the individual involved. However, after leaving the physical body, you will immediately find yourself in another. This is the same kind of form in which you travel in out-of-body projections, and again let me remind my readers that each of them leaves the body for some time each night during sleep.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第537节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "537", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0113", "zh": "不过，在你睡眠时，你的意识经常的溜出你的身体又回去。当你在你身体之外时你做梦，就像你在它里面做梦一样，因而，你可以形成关于你自己的出体旅行的“梦故事”，而你的肉体形象在床上沉睡。你看：未知的实相对你而言并非真的那么神秘，你只假装它是。有时候，你对你的旅程有相当清楚的感知，但你探访的那实际当地领域与你自己的世界是如此不同，以至于你试着尽你所能的以通常状况的观点去诠释它们。万一你记得一个插曲，它也会显得非常混乱，因为你会把你自己的世界观置于它不属于的地方。", "en": "In your sleep, however, your consciousness slips out of your body and returns to it frequently. You dream when you are out of your body, even as you dream inside it. You may therefore form dream stories about your own out-of-body travel, while your physical image rests soundly in bed. The unknown reality, you see, is not really that mysterious to you. You only pretend that it is. Sometimes you have quite clear perceptions of your journeys, but the actual native territories that you visit are so different from your own world that you try to interpret them as best you can in the light of usual conditions. If you remember such an episode at all it may well seem very confusing, for you will have superimposed your own world view where it does not belong.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第719节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "719", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0062", "zh": "当然，只是因为大多数人相信你不能离开你的身体，所以在你的一生里，你才不常常有意识地有“出体”的经验。这种经验远比文字能够使你对你所将遭遇的情况有个了解。", "en": "Of course, it is only because most people believe that you cannot leave your body that you do not consciously have out-of-body experiences with any frequency, generally speaking, in your lifetimes. Such experiences would acquaint you far better than words with some understanding of the conditions that will be encountered.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第536节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "536", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0109", "zh": "每晚当你睡觉时，你本能的离开身体不同长短的时间，但那些旅程并非被“计划好的”，换言之，你计划你自己的观光。就像具有同样兴趣的许多人可能决定参加观光团，去一起探访同样的国家，因此，在出体状态时你也许一个人或与同伴相偕而行。如果你警觉的话，你甚至可能拍些照片——只不过就内在观光而言，那些照片包括了在当时拍的关于环境的清晰画面，在无意识里冲洗好，而后呈现给清醒的心智。", "en": "Instinctively you leave your body for varying amounts of time each night while you sleep, but those journeys are not “programmed.” You plan your own tours, in other words. As many people with the same interests may decide to visit the same country together, on tour, so in the out-of-body condition you may travel alone or with companions. If you are alert you may even take snapshots — only as far as inner tours are concerned, the snapshots consist of clear pictures of the environment taken at the time, developed in the unconscious, and then presented to the waking mind.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第710节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "710", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "记不住不是失败：醒着的那部分没跟着走", "note": "赛斯解释了一个很机械的原因：你平时主要透过自己的肉体机制来知觉你的意识，所以当意识不经肉体媒介运作时——像出体，以及一些离魂的情况——你对它就几乎没有觉知。第二个原因更麻烦：即使在较深的梦和相当不寻常的投射里你们确实完全离开了自己的系统，人还是想用那套学来的模式去转译经验，而不切换到内在感官，这就是许多这类经验即使回想起来也显得混乱而无意义的原因。因此他把关键动作放在练习上：暗示自己把醒时的意识带进睡眠状态，对有意识的出体投射特别有价值，习惯性地运用就会成功；他还直说这正是你们不记得那些完全正当的投射的原因。仪器帮不上忙——他的说法是，意识里缺席的那部分无法由脑波模式追踪，只有在离开与回来的那一点可能显出一个特殊模式，出体本身用任何方法都侦查不到。", "src": "第 534、467、492、571 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 534 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 467 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 492 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 571 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0060", "zh": "我们再继续口授。（停顿，许多次中之一。）意识有许多特性，你们当然已知道某一些，不过，还有许多并不那么明显，因为你目前大半是以这样的一种方式用你的意识，以致于它的知觉显得十分不“自然”的样子。换言之，你透过你自己的肉体机制来知觉你的意识。当你的意识不经由肉体的媒介来运作时，如它在“出体”以及一些“离魂”的情况时，你对它就不大知觉了。", "en": "We will resume dictation. (Pause; one of many.) Consciousness has many characteristics, some of course known to you. Many of the characteristics of consciousness, however, are not so apparent, since presently you largely use your own consciousness in such a way that its perceptions appear in quite other than “natural” guises. You are aware of your own consciousness, in other words, through the medium of your own physical mechanism. You are not nearly as aware of your own consciousness when it is not operating primarily through the mediumship of the body, as it does in out-of-body states and some dissociated conditions.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第534节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "534", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0034", "zh": "在较深的梦里和相当不寻常的出体投射里，你们能够——而且确实——完全离开你们自己的系统。然而即使出了物质身体，你们仍会试图用那套学来的模式来转译经验，而不会切换到内在感官。这就是为什么许多这类经验，即使回想起来，也显得混乱而无意义。", "en": "In deeper dreams and fairly unusual projections, you can and do leave your own system entirely. Even though you are out of your physical body however, you will attempt to translate experience with its learned patterns rather than switching into the inner senses. This is why many such experiences, even if recalled, seem chaotic and without meaning.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第467节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "467", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0039", "zh": "他已经找到了你们的位置，他会来的。或者，你们也可能在梦里以一个强烈的幻象相当清楚地看见他；若是如此，他会自报身份。然而，对任何这类工作来说，开始训练自己把醒时的意识带着进入睡眠，是极为重要的。这正是你们不记得那些完全正当的出体投射的原因。", "en": "He has found your location, and he will be here. You may instead quite clearly see him in a strong vision within a dream. If so he will announce himself. It is highly important however for any such work that you begin to train yourself to take your waking consciousness with you in sleep. It is the reason why you do not remember quite legitimate projections you have made.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第492节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "492", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0071", "zh": "意识的以肉体为依归的那部分留在身体内，同时较高的直觉中心则被激发起来。自己的那个“缺席”部分不能由脑波模式来追踪，虽然在它离开与回来的那一点可能显出一个特殊的模式。可是，“出体”的本身无法用任何方法侦查到，画的线只显示在离开前的那一刻所显示的任何具特征性的模式。", "en": "The higher centers of intuition are activated while physically oriented portions of consciousness remain with the body. The “absent” portion of the self cannot be traced through brain patterns, though the point of its departure and the point of its return may show a particular pattern. The “time out” itself, however, will not be detected in any way, the tracings showing only whatever characteristic pattern was being given immediately before departure.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第569节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "569", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "出去了，你还是有一个身体", "note": "赛斯说，为了所有实际的目的，你会在出体经验中发现自己处于某种身体形式——不是变成一缕没有形状的意识。他把这个说法讲得更细：当你以任意一种出体经验离开肉体时，你实际上是离开它、进入一个只比它稍微不那么具体的身体；这个身体后来也依次被换掉，换成更不具体的，但形体这个概念作为象征太重要，所以它在你们所有的宗教文学与来世故事里一路被带着走。他也给了一条限制：你投射出去的那个形式并不是真正完整的形式，因为一定要有某种生命力的划分，肉体才能够在出体期间维持存在。回来的通道同样是实打实的：这类经验全部用到一种化学能量，化学反应造成意识与肉体之间的电磁连结，没有它就没有回到肉体这一说，而使化学能量成为可能的又是心智能量，所以意识的这份自由并不依赖物质存在。身体那边并没有停机，它维持自己的平衡，有点像一个维护站。", "src": "第 261、331、571、709 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 261 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 331 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 571 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 709 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0008", "zh": "有几个重点我想说一下。为了所有实际的目的，你会在出体经验中发现你自己处于某种身体形式。", "en": "（One minute pause.） There are several points I would like to make. For all practical purposes, you will find yourself in some sort of body form in your out-of-body experiences.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第261节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "261", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0072", "zh": "在大多数的意识阶段里，你会用到你具有一个身体的概念。当你在任意一种“出体”经验里离开了你的肉体时，你实际上是在一个较它只稍微不那么具体的身体里离开它。这个身体“后来”也依次被舍弃而有个更不具体的身体，但“形体”的概念是个这么重要的象征，以致在你们所有的宗教性文学与来世的故事里都一直带着它。", "en": "You will use the idea of a body in most stages of consciousness. When you leave your physical body in any kind of out-of-body experience, you actually leave it in another that is only slightly less physical. This in turn is “later” discarded for one still less physical, but the idea of the form is so important a symbol that you carry it through all of your religious literature, and stories of hereafter.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第571节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "571", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0024", "zh": "在平常的状况下，还有肉体形式中的那些人不会感知它。这种形式很像你投射的形式，但是你投射的形式并不是真正完整的形式，因为一定要有某种（划线）生命力的划分，这样才能够在出体期间维持肉体的存在。", "en": "Under usual conditions it will not be perceived by those still in physical form. This form is much like the form in which you project, but the form which you project is not truly complete, for there must be some (underlined) division of vitality so that physical existence is maintained during out-of-body episodes.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第331节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "331", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0010", "zh": "然而，在这类出体经验中，全部都使用了一种化学能量。化学反应导致意识和肉体之间产生电磁连结，没有它，用你们的话来说，就不会回到肉体。但是，当然，使化学能量成为可能的，是心智能量。你知道，这种意识的自由并不依赖物质存在。", "en": "However there is a chemical energy used in all such out-of-body experiences. The chemical reaction results in an electromagnetic connection between the consciousness and the physical body, and without it there would be no return to the physical body, in your terms. Of course it is mental energy that makes the chemical energy possible, however. This freedom of consciousness is not dependent upon physical existence, you see.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第261节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "261", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0103", "zh": "这样一个旅行中的意识也许会在物质实相里旅游：虽然没有以通常的方式与那系统相连，它仍可以是与之联盟的。从那观点，物质本身将会看起来与普通的样子不同。在另一方面，一个出体意识也可能进入其它物质取向的实相：那些“以不同于你们自己的频率运作的实相”。意识之基本上独立的本质容许这样子的脱离。身体意识维持住它自己的平衡，而有点像一个维护站一样。", "en": "Such a traveling consciousness may journey within physical reality, colon: While not relating to that system in the usual manner, it may still be allied with it. From that viewpoint matter itself will seem to appear differently than it does ordinarily. On the other hand, an out-of-body consciousness may also enter other physically attuned realities: those operating “at different frequencies than your own.” The basically independent nature of consciousness allows for such disentanglement.5 The body consciousness maintains its own equilibrium, and acts somewhat like a maintenance station.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第709节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "709", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "出体和死亡走同一条路，差别只在连结有没有断", "note": "这是这一页最安抚人的一条。赛斯说，当意识离开身体、走开了有好一段时间，联系当然就断了；在出体的情况，联系仍然在——这条线还连着，就是出去的人会回来的理由。他同时给了一个警告：一个已死的人如果几乎只与自己的肉体形象认同，可能完全误解死亡经验，试图再进入那具尸体。自我之所以对出体戒慎恐惧，正因为它把出体永远读成肉体的死亡；可是赛斯说，在成功的投射之后，自我会变得更有自信，因为它发现自己不仅完整无缺，还充实到无法估量。他还透露接引死者熟悉处境的那一队荣誉卫士里，活着的成员就是在肉体睡眠时以出体的方式来执行这些活动的，因为他们熟悉意识的投射及其所涉及的感觉。出体也常常把人带进一个不同于尘俗的、或极美而壮观的环境，这类来自那一层的经验几乎都以象征出现，否则对你毫无意义。", "src": "第 537、279、535、575 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 537 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 279 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 535 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 575 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0063", "zh": "当意识离开了身体，走开了有好一段时间，那么联系当然就断了。在“出体”的情况联系仍然在。那么一个已死的人很可能完全误解了死亡经验而试图再进入尸体。当此人几乎唯独与他的肉体形象认同时，可能发生这种事情。", "en": "When consciousness leaves the body and is away for some time then the connection is, of course, broken. In out-of-body states the connection still holds. Now it is possible for an individual who has died to completely misinterpret the experience and attempt to reenter the corpse. This can happen when the personality identified himself almost exclusively with the physical image.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第537节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "537", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0014", "zh": "一般来说，自我对这样的行为是戒慎恐惧的，因为对它来说，出体经验永远象征着肉体的死亡。同时，在成功投射之后，自我变得更有自信，因为它发现自己不仅完整无缺而且还充实到无法估量的程度。事实上，自我对于任何创造行为都是既抗拒、恐惧又渴望。任何创造行为，包括任何艺术的创作在内，都需要暂时摆脱自我，逃离自我，这就是自我害怕的事。", "en": "The ego, as a rule, is frightfully leery of such action, since to it an out-of body experience always symbolizes physical death. At the same time the ego becomes more assured after successful projections, since ir discovers itself not only intact but immeasurably enriched. Indeed, the ego both fights, fears and desires any creative act. Any creative act, including the production of any art, necessitates a momentary release from the ego, an escape from it, which the ego fears.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第279节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "279", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0061", "zh": "这种荣誉卫士是以你们说来还活着或已死的人所组成的。那些活在你们的实相系统里面的人，当肉体在睡眠时，在“出体”的经验里面执行这些活动。他们熟悉意识的投射及其其所涉及的感觉，而他们帮助那些不再回到肉体的人熟悉这一切。", "en": "Now this honorary guard is made up of people in your terms both living and dead. Those who are living in your system of reality perform these activities in an “out-of-body” experience while the physical body sleeps. They are familiar with the projection of consciousness, with the sensations involved, and they help orient those who will not be returning to the physical body.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第535节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "535", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0073", "zh": "几乎所有从这层面来的经验都将以“象征”来代表，因为若非如此它们对你将毫无意义。这些经验多少都与非物质性的生命、非肉身的意识与形式，以及独立于物质之外的意识有关。这些经验对你永远有支持性。在这儿常常涉及了“出体”的经验，在其中投射者发现自己在一个不同于尘俗的或一个极美且壮观的环境里。", "en": "Almost all experiences from this level will be symbolically represented, for otherwise they would have no meaning to you. The experiences will all have to do in one way or another with nonphysical life, noncorporeal consciousness and forms, and the independence of consciousness from matter. These experiences will always be supportive. Out-of-body experiences will often be involved here, in which the projectionist finds himself in an unearthly environment or one of great beauty and grandeur.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第575节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "575", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "出去了，时间和空间就换了规则", "note": "赛斯把出体讲成时空关系的改变，而不是位置的移动。他说，哪怕你只是离开身体在几尺之内走动，意识与那个房间的关系已经不同了，那个人与时空的关系也已经换了；出体状态的时间按你们的标准是额外的时间，你不会变老。同一段他还说，出体经验其实有利健康——系统自动放松、摆脱压力的束缚，也不受时间约束，身体在暂停中不会老化，全程没有用到肉体感官，感知当下旅行中的意识用内在感官，并自动做出必要的调整好让自我能用习惯的方式接收资料。至于距离，他讲得更直接：你的感官关于物质本质的报告完全错误，关于空间的观念也一样错；在活着时的出体经验里遇到的许多空间问题，死后也会遇到，经过空间不必费时间，空间不以距离存在，确实有阻碍，但那些是精神上的阻碍，有些经验的强度在你们的实相里才被诠释成几里几里。他也说在出体状态意识能旅行得比光还快，事实上常常是瞬间发生的，某些梦和出体经验里因此能感知到质量或物质的其他形式。", "src": "第 709、292、537、581 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 709 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 292 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 537 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 581 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0102", "zh": "从你们平时的观点，旅行中的意识是在焦点外的，而没有以指定的方式锁定在物质的坐标里。可是，所谓的内在世界，至少在理论上来说，可以以这样一种方式探索。意识有一阵子使它自己由它通常的坐标里“解开”，当这发生时，出体的旅行者不只是离开了他的肉体形式。那个人踏出了适当的范围。即使当一个人离开了身体，而只不过漫游到离身体几尺之远的地方也有些改变——意识与那房间的关系不同了，那个个人与时空的关系已改变了。以你们的标准，出体的时间是“额外的时间”，举例来说，你不会变老，虽然这效应按照某些原则而有所不同。我以后还会提到这些。", "en": "From your ordinary point of view the traveling consciousness is off-focus, not locked into physical coordinates in the designated fashion. The so-called inner world can be at least theoretically explored, however, in just such a way. Consciousness “unlocks” itself for a while from its usual coordinates. When this happens the out-of-body traveler is not simply out of his or her corporal form. The person steps out of usual context. Even if an individual leaves the body and wanders about the room no more than a few feet away from where the body is located,3 there are alterations, dash — the relationship of consciousness to the room is different. The relationship of the individual to time and space has altered. Time out of the body is “free time” by your standards. You do not age, for example, although this effect varies according to certain principles. I will mention these later.4", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第709节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "709", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0015", "zh": "在梦中，当你什么都不预期时，就什么都不会出现。出体经验其实是有利健康的。你的系统自动放松，摆脱压力的束缚。还有，顺便一提，也不受时间的约束。在投射期间，它不会老化；也就是说，身体不会老化。它在暂停中。任何解读都是意识本身所做的解读。没有用到肉体感官，没有两字画线。在感知的当下，旅行中的意识透过内在感官来感知，并且靠它自己自动做出必要的调整，好让自我能够以它习惯的方式感知资料。", "en": "In dreams, when you expect none, none appear. Out of body experiences indeed can be a health boon. Your system is automatically relaxed and free of pressure. Also, incidentally, free of time. It does not age during a projection; that is, the body does not age. It is in suspension. Any interpretations that are made are made by consciousness itself. The physical senses are not， underline not, utilized. At the moment of perception the traveling consciousness perceives through the inner senses, and by itself automatically makes the necessary adjustments so that the ego can perceive the data in its accustomed way.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第292节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "292", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0065", "zh": "举例来说，既然你的感知机制坚持物体是固态的，因此它们坚持像“空间”这样的一件东西是存在的。其实你的感官所告诉你关于物质的本质是完全错误的，而它们告诉你关于“空间”的观念也是一样的错——对基本真实来说是错的，但当然跟三次元观念是符合的。（幽默地：）在活着时的“出体”经验中，遭遇到许多与“空间”有关的问题，在死后也会遇到。所以，在这些插曲里，“时间”与“空间”的真正性质变得更明显了。例如，在死后，经过“空间”不必费“时间”。“空间”也不以距离的说法存在。时、空都是幻觉。的确有阻碍存在，但都是精神或心灵上的阻碍。例如，有些经验的强度在你的实相里是以几里几里的距离来诠释的。", "en": "As your perceptive mechanisms insist that objects are solid, for example, so they insist that such a thing as space exists. Now what your senses tell you about the nature of matter is entirely erroneous, and what they tell you about space is equally wrong — wrong in terms of basic reality, but quite in keeping of course with three-dimensional concepts. (Humorously): In out-of-body experiences from the living state, many of the problems are encountered, in terms of space, that will be met after death. And in such episodes, therefore, the true nature of time and space becomes more apparent. After death it does not take time to go through space, for example. Space does not exist in terms of distance. This is illusion. There are barriers, but they are mental or psychic barriers. For example, there are intensities of experience that are interpreted in your reality as distance in miles.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第537节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "537", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0101", "zh": "当透过身体结构运作时，如你们自己的这种意识大半聚焦在三度空间取向上。不过，在出体状态时意识能旅行得比光还快——事实上，这常常是瞬间发生的。", "en": "(Pause, one of many, at 9:37.) While operating through the body structures, consciousnesses such as your own focus largely upon the three-dimensional orientation. In out-of-body states, however, consciousness can travel faster than light — often, in fact, instantaneously.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第709节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "709", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0075", "zh": "不过，你的意识也有能在其他场所创造实相的配备。在某些梦中或“出体”的经验里，你自己的意识移动得比光速还快，在这种情况下你能感知到某些这种“质量或物质”的其他形式。", "en": "(Pause at 9:40.) Your consciousness, however, is equipped to create realities in other fields as well. Now in certain dreams and out-of-body experiences, your own consciousness moves faster than the speed of light, and under such conditions you are able to perceive some of these other forms of “mass or matter.”", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第581节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "581", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "你在那里看见的，一半是环境，一半是你的信念", "note": "赛斯对「那算不算真的」这个问题给的回答很特别：你在梦中或出体经验里看到的物体、拜访的地方，基本上和任何实质物体或地点一样真实，因为两者基本上都不是真实的，当然也不是不真实的；内在感官不扭曲资料，但你一旦想把资料交给自我，某种程度的扭曲就必然进来。更要紧的是你的经验跟随着你的期望走，这条在死后、梦里和任何出体的遭遇里都适用——执迷于恶的概念就会碰上恶的情况，相信魔鬼就会碰见它，却不知那是你自己创造的心念形相。所以他明确说，在任何出神或出体状态都没有理由接触到妖魔鬼怪：那是你自己的幻觉使你看不见它们被投射进去的环境；同样的机制会把一次进入实相其他层面的出体经验变成一次天堂之游，把你自己更大本质那还不被认识的声音听成神、宇宙人或先知的声音。他也点名的确有人在做相反的事：有些书教人计划出体活动，让上百万人被告以离开身体就会碰到这个恶魔或那个愤怒的神明，所以他反过来提议在内心实相里建一座旅行者都能来的自由城市，当作对他们创造能力的一个大得多的挑战。", "src": "第 266、538、710、744、758 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 266 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 538 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 710 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 758 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0012", "zh": "在梦中或出体经验中，你将看到的物体以及你将拜访的地方基本上和任何实质物体或地点一样真实，因为两者基本上都不是真实的。它们当然也不是不真实。一旦你开始转译一个意念，你就在扭曲它了。你看，内在感官不会扭曲资料，但是当你试图让自我能够得到这样的资料时，一定程度的扭曲就会进入其中。", "en": "The objects that you will see and the places that you will visit, in dream or out-of-body experiences, are basically as real as any physical object or location, because neither are basically real. Nor of course are they unreal. As soon as you begin to translate an idea you are distorting it. The inner senses you see do not distort the data, but when you attempt to make such data available to the ego, then distortion to some extent must enter in.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第266节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "266", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0066", "zh": "换言之，你的经验跟随着你的期望走。在死后与梦中的经验以及任何“出体”的遭遇中，这个原则也适用。如果你执迷于恶的概念，那你就会碰上恶的情况。如果你相信魔鬼，那你就会碰见它。如我先前提过的，当意识不是针对着肉体时，它有更大的自由。再说一次，思想和感情不经过时间流逝就建构实相。因此如果你相信你会遇上一个恶魔，你就会创造出这样的一个“心念形相”来，却不知它乃是你自己的创造物。", "en": "Your experience, in other words, follows your expectations. Now the same applies to after-death experience and to the dream experience, and to any out-of-body encounters. If you are obsessed with the idea of evil, then you will meet evil conditions. If you believe in devils, then you will encounter these. As I mentioned earlier, there is greater freedom when consciousness is not physically directed. Thoughts and emotions are constructed, again, into reality without the physical time lapse. So if you believe you will be met by a demon, you will create your own thought-form of one, not realizing that it is of your own creation.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第538节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "538", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0110", "zh": "不过，那种建构也造成了一个损害，因为它阻止你与你自己原创性的观念接触。举例来说，在任何出神或出体状态都没有理由接触到任何的妖魔鬼怪。（停顿。）在这种例子里，你自己的幻觉使你看不见它们被投射进去的环境，那么，当你的意识不是直接集中焦点在物质实相时，心灵的伟大创造力被给予了充分的发挥。当你学会随身带着你“正常警醒的”意识心时，心灵所有的次元都忠实的，并且即刻的变成了经验；而当你脱出这种局限性概念时，那么，在那些层面你能看到你自己心灵的内在力量，而观赏在你眼前展现的信念与象征的相互作用。除非你学会这样做，否则你一定会有困难，因为你将不能分辨你的投射及在内在环境里所发生的事之间的不同。", "en": "That kind of structuring also does a disservice, however, for it prevents you from coming in contact with your own original concepts. There is no reason, for example, to encounter any demons or devils in any trance or out-of-body condition.3 (Pause.) In such cases your own hallucinations blind you to the environment within which they are projected. When your consciousness is not directly focused in physical reality, then, the great creativity of the psyche is given fuller play. All of its dimensions are faithfully and instantly produced as experience when you learn to take your “normally alert” conscious mind with you; and when you are free of such limiting ideas, then at those levels you can glimpse the inner powers of your own psyche, and watch the interplay of beliefs and symbols as they are manifested before your eyes. Until you learn to do this you will most certainly have difficulty, for you will not be able to tell the difference between your projections and what is happening in the inner environment.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第710节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "710", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0120", "zh": "因此，这些梦往往就像安排好的戏，在其中你已熟悉的道具来掩饰这种造访。当你经验到不同凡响的灵感闪现时，或感知其它非官方的资料时，这类的事常常发生。你迅速地试着使这种数据合乎常理。例如，一次进入实相其它层面的出体（out-of- body）经验，变成一次天堂之游。或直到现在未被认出的、你自己更大的本质的声音，变成了神、或宇宙人、或先知的声音。", "en": "So, often such dreams are like programmed dramas, in that you clothe such visitations in familiar props. The same sort of thing frequently occurs when you experience extraordinary flashes of inspiration, or perceive other unofficial data. Quickly you try to make sense of such material in usual terms. An out-of-body experience into another level of reality becomes a visit to heaven, for example; or the heretofore-unrecognized voice of your own greater identity becomes the voice of God, or a spaceman or prophet.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第758节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "758", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0117", "zh": "有一些教人计划出体活动的书：你们上百万的人被告以，当你们离开你们的身体时，你们会碰到这个或那个恶魔、这个或那个愤怒的神明。所以，反之，我们将形成一个那些旅行者可以来的自由城市，而在那儿，如果他们喜欢的话，他们可以读有关佛教的书或扮演一个天主教徒的角色。在这城市四周还会设下某些心爱的陷阱，那是具有一种让人开悟的性质……现在听好：你们认为在你们的空间里建造一座平台在本质上并非不可能的……那么，我建议的是，在内心实相里的一个平台。以具体说法而言，它就与在天空里绕着轨道转的一个城市一样有效——甚至更有效，而它是对你们创造能力的一个大得多的挑战。你们需要一个好的挑战——那是很好玩的：并不因为你们应该做它，却因为你们渴望它…… 它是一个你们可以从你们未来的自己抛给你们的一个了不起的创造性挑战。", "en": "Now there are books programming out-of-body activity; millions of you are told that when you leave your body you will meet this demon or that demon, or this or that angry god. So, instead, we will form a free city to which those travelers can come, and where those who enter can read books about Buddhism if they prefer, or play at being Catholic. There will also be certain beloved traps set about the city, that will be of an enlightening nature … Now listen: You think there is nothing intrinsically impossible about building a platform in [your] space … I am suggesting, then, a platform in inner reality. It is as valid — far more valid — as an orbiting city in the sky, in physical terms, and it challenges your creative abilities much more. You need a good challenge — it is fun! Not because you should do it, but because you desire it … It is a great creative challenge that you can throw down to yourselves from your future selves.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "赛斯推荐的做法，日常到几乎不像修法", "note": "赛斯最推荐的一个入口是半夜那一下：当你醒来、或似乎在半夜时，干脆尝试出体，只要试着离开床，在肉体留在原处时走进另一个房间——他说这个方法非常值得用。理由很实际：这种练习比突如其来的投射更不会吓到自我，而走进隔壁房间这种日常动作的性质也比较叫人安心，你比较冷静，而且还在自己的环境里。第二条是暗示：把醒时的意识带进睡眠，习惯性运用就会成功，因为不带走它正是那些正当投射不被记得的原因。他还给了结伴出体的对暗号方式：对方若只看见你的肉体，就该向你开口、宣告他自己已经出体、邀你前去会合；你若还在身内而且条件良好，便会出体与他汇合；若没有回应，那就是你自己正在进行无意识的投射，而建立起星光接触之后也许需要一些操运来维持，但就算各走各路也无需担心。赛斯要他们认认真真把出体旅行发展成一项爱好，说动机够强就没有理由练不成，会发现有各种各样的人可以做榜样；他也预告进度会长什么样：在你觉知到出去的那个机制之前，大概会有好几回是你回过神来了，才意识到自己曾经投射出去。", "src": "第 298、492、497、503 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 298 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 492 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 497 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 503 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0018", "zh": "鲁柏最近邂逅卡拉汉的经验是相当确实的。他在自己完全不知情的状况下，使用了一个有利的投射方法，我非常推荐你们两人使用这个方法。当你醒来，或似乎在半夜时，就干脆尝试出体。只要试着离开床，你看，在肉体留在原处时，走进另一个房间。", "en": "Ruburt’s experience with your Miss Callahan recently was quite legitimate. He used a most advantageous method of projection without knowing that he did so, and I highly recommend this method to you both. When you awaken, or seem to in the middle of the night, try simply to get out of the physical body. Simply try to get out of bed, you see, and to walk into another room while the physical body stays where it is.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第298节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "298", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0019", "zh": "这个练习一定比突如其来的投射更不会吓到自我，而且活动的日常性质，比方说，走进隔壁房间，也会比较令人安心。你比较冷静，而且是在你自己的环境里。看到卡拉汉小姐的时候，鲁柏当然是出体了，而卡拉汉小姐状况也是一样。", "en": "The experience will be must less startling to the ego than an abrupt projection, and the ordinary nature of the activities, walking into the next room for example, will be reassuring. You are more calm, and in your own surroundings. Of course Ruburt was out of his body when he saw Miss Callahan, who was in the same condition.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第298节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "298", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0038", "zh": "而那条把醒时意识带进睡眠状态的暗示，对有意识的出体投射特别有价值——只要你们肯运用它。你们若习惯性地运用它，就会成功。", "en": "Now the suggestion to carry your waking consciousness into the sleep state is of particular value in Conscious projections, if you will use it. You would succeed if you use it habitually.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第492节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "492", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0044", "zh": "如果他只看见你的物质身体，他就该向你开口，宣告他自己已经出体，邀你前来会合。你若还在身内，而且条件良好，你便会出体与他汇合。若没有回应，那就是你自己正在进行无意识的投射。建立起星光接触之后，也许需要一些操运来维持接触；不过就算你们各走各路，也并无心配。", "en": "If he only sees your physical body then he should address you, announce his own out-of-body state and invite you to join him. If you are still in your body and if conditions are good, you will then leave your body and join him. If there is no response then you are on an unconscious projection of your own. When astral contact is made, some manipulations may be necessary in order to maintain them, but there is nothing to worry about if you go your separate ways.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第497节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "497", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0040", "zh": "我希望你们认认真真地把出体旅行发展成一项爱好。只要动机够强烈，你们没有理由练不成。你们会发现有各种各样的人可以为你们做榜样。而伴随其间的意识改变，也会让你们得以做出几次明确的、有利的焦点转换，与你们自己的工作相呼应。", "en": "I would like you to seriously embark upon the hobby of out-of-body travel. There is no reason why you cannot become proficient at it if you are strongly enough motivated. You will find all kinds of people that can serve as models for you. The alteration of consciousness involved will also enable you to make several distinct and advantageous changes of focus, in line with your own work.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第497节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "497", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0052", "zh": "照可能性的现状来看，从现在到初冬，你们两个人都会在出体工作上大有进展。（对我：）你出体运作的程度远超过去；如今不久，你就该获得有意识的觉知。在你觉知到出去的那个机制之前，你大概会有好几回，回过神来，意识到自己曾经投射出去。", "en": "As the probabilities exist, both of you will be well into the out-of-body work between now and early winter. (To me:) you have been operating far more than in the past, and you should shortly now gain conscious awareness. You will probably come to, realizing you have projected, several times, before becoming conscious of the mechanism of getting out.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第503节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "503", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "害怕是正常的，节奏由你自己踩", "note": "赛斯在教做法之前先把安全说明讲完：他说自己特别关注投射这件事，正因为你们自己的能力会很快把你们推向那个方向，所以除非你知道自己在做什么，否则他不希望你们两个四处旅行。他的安抚也很直白：不要因为那个领域里任何新的发展而害怕，无论你知道还是不知道他都会在场；外头并没有什么幽灵，那只不过是一处新的环境，会安全返回，一路都有保护——他甚至说本想牵着对方的手，可那恐怕比什么都更会让人害怕。为什么有时实验会失败？他的解释是当事人在出体实验里始终在他的保护之下，除了自己的态度之外没有东西能阻止他看见赛斯，而自我在这件事上是帮忙的，会确保过度耗用不发生，实验失败通常就是这个原因。他也说过在出体的努力里，若真陷于严重困境本来会有人来帮忙，但为了他自己的信心，最好还是让他自己走到底。最后是他给的个人化线索：追踪自己在日常生活中与梦里显现的种种象征，把象征和它所代表的感受连起来，某些象征会在特定的意识层次出现，成为你自己探索里的识别点——例如有的人快要出体时总会梦到一间可以到处摸、到处搞的屋子或公寓；也有的人每次出去都先进入阿尔法状态，却不在那个门口停留，直接从那里起飞。", "src": "第 265、457、460、471、571、573 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 265 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 457 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 460 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 471 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 571 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 573 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0011", "zh": "我们特别关注的是，你看，投射这件事，只是因为你们自己的能力会很快引导你们走向那个方向。因此，只要是我能够给你们的资讯，都会带来很大的实际助益。除非你知道自己在做什么，否则我不希望你两个四处（出体）旅行。", "en": "I am particularly concerned, you see, with this matter of projection, simply because your own abilities will rather swiftly lead you along in that direction. Therefore whatever information I can give you will be of great practical benefit. I do not want either of you traveling about unless you know what you are doing.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第265节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "265", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0031", "zh": "一小注。我相信，鲁柏在出体经验上会有额外的自由。告诉他：不要因为那个领域里任何新的发展而害怕。无论他知道还是不知道，我都会在场。不，外头并没有什么幽灵，鲁柏。那只不过是一处新的环境。你们会安全返回的。有位朋友想结识你——我的朋友。一段短时间里的长途旅程。一路都会有保护。我本想牵着你的手，可那恐怕比什么都更会让你害怕。请放心，那会是一趟安全的旅程。", "en": "One small note. I believe there will be extra freedom in out-of-body experiences for Ruburt. Tell him not to be frightened at any new developments in that area. I will be there whether he knows it or not. No, there are not any phantoms out there, Ruburt. It will simply be a new environment. You will return safely. A friend wants to meet you. My friend. A long trip in a brief time. You will be protected all the way. I would hold your hand, but that would probably frighten you more than anything else. Be assured, it will be a safe trip.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第457节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "457", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0032", "zh": "现在。鲁柏在做出体实验时，始终在我的保护之下。在那样的场合，除了他自己的态度之外，没有什么能阻止他看见我——我先前说过。不过他是按自然的速率在进步，按他自己的速率。他不会做过头，因为在这件事上他的自我是帮忙的，它会确保过度耗用的事不发生。当实验失败时，这通常就是原因，那也就是节奏性效应的缘由。", "en": "Now. Ruburt is always under my protection in his out-of-body experiments. There is nothing to prevent his seeing me on such occasions but his own attitude, as I have said before. He progresses at a natural rate however, at his own rate. He will not overdo, for in this his ego is an aid and it will see to it that overexertion does not occur. When experiments fail this is usually the reason, and also the reason for the rhythmic effect.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第460节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "460", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0035", "zh": "在任何出体的努力里，或在任何别的尘外实相里，这都会保护他。他其实已经变得相当取巧了，而这份成就虽然用错了方向，也显示了他能力的成长。若他真的陷于严重的困境，本会有人来帮他的。他有许多朋友，但最好还是让他自己走到底，为了他自己的信心。", "en": "This will always protect him in any out of body endeavors, or any other unearthly realities. He was actually getting rather tricky, and the accomplishment, while misguided, shows the growth of his abilities. Now had he been in severe difficulties someone would, have helped him. He has many friends, but it was best that he followed through on his own for his own confidence.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第471节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "471", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0086", "zh": "显然你现在无法了解到那种层次的意识是何等境界，但是你却可以借由追踪自己日常生活中与梦中所显现的种种“象征”，并设法将“象征”与“象征所代表的感受”连接起来，以发现某些特定的“象征”与自己在不同的意识层次中的关系，“象征”往往是你自己的追寻表现在“象征”上的反应。例如在鲁柏的情形中，当他在梦中将要出体的时候，他常常会梦到自己置身在一个又像房子，又像公寓的屋子里，而这个屋子里有的是各种各样让他东摸西搞的机会。", "en": "Obviously you cannot become aware of that stage of consciousness now, but you can keep track of the way symbols appear to you in both waking life and the dream state, and learn to connect them with the feelings they represent. You will learn that certain symbols will appear personally to you at various stages of consciousness, and these can serve as points of recognition in your own explorations. When Ruburt is about to leave his body from the dream state for example, he will often find himself in a strange house or apartment that offers opportunities for exploration.", "source": "时空之外 · 第571节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "571", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0087", "zh": "典型的状态是，每当他要出体的时候，他都先进入阿尔法状态，但却不在这个门中停留，而直接由此处进入更深的层次。", "en": "Characteristically, when he leaves his body he does the same thing, hardly pausing at the threshold of alpha but taking off from there.", "source": "时空之外 · 第573节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "573", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "出体给你的是一双肉体没有的眼睛", "note": "赛斯讲出体的感知红利讲得非常具体：除非你从出体的状态里看过，你就不曾真正见过彩虹的颜色；要看一朵花的颜色、一个苹果的颜色，就必须走出身体；除非你出体去看一张蜘蛛网，甚至从蜘蛛的观点去看它，你就不曾见过什么叫图案设计。他的解释是，就像地球的大气把你的科学家挡在宇宙的情况之外，身体的情况也同样叫你对真正的色彩与图案视而不见——不过他也补了一句，身体是一架顶方便的工具，不建议在它外面待太久。内在感官本来就是为感知非实质资料而准备的，不被你投射入三次元实相的影像欺骗，也能感知实质物体，而你在出体经验里用的正是它们。他还说在某些出体经验里看见的颜色比任何实质颜色都更眩目，那是内在感官所感知的较大光谱的一部分。对画画的人他给了一个玩法：出体状态里思想几乎瞬间就变成某种可塑的类物质，你们可以试着把意识投进自己所画的环境，特别去观察那里不曾熟悉的色彩层次与形形色色的空间关系，再设法在作品里重现它们。他说这些修习会在一切其他方面帮助你们，让你们极为切身地结识其他实相，并为终将没有可供操运的物质身体的那段时期预作准备。", "src": "第 501、539、900、497 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 501 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 539 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 900 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 497 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0050", "zh": "你也可以在心灵活动与你感兴趣的那两样东西——色彩与绘画——之间，找到许多关联。现在我告诉你：除非你从出体的状态里看过，你就不曾真正见过彩虹的颜色。如果你想看一朵花的颜色，或者，我亲爱的朋友们，一个苹果的颜色，你就必须走出身体才能看到。你不必觉得他的心灵能力把你排除在外，也不必觉得你自己没有能力：更不必觉得他的能力会把他从你身边拉走，因为它们只会把他带得更近。你自己的能力在这里，也是要用的，而且要用你自己独有的方式去用。", "en": "You can also find many connections between psychic activity and color and painting in which you are interested. Now I will tell you, you have never seen the colors of a rainbow unless you have seen them from an out-of-body state. If you want to see the colors of a flower, or my dear friends, of an apple, you must get out of your body to do so. Now you do not need to feel that his psychic abilities close you out, or that you do not have your own: or that his abilities will draw him away from you, for they would only bring him closer. Your own abilities are here to be used also, and in your own unique fashion.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第501节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "501", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0051", "zh": "除非你出体去看一张蜘蛛网，你就不曾见过什么叫作图案设计。除非你从蜘蛛的观点去看一张蜘蛛网，你就不曾见过什么叫作图案设计。现在，这是能学会的。你可以用你的心灵能力，把你的意识投进蜘蛛里面。你的身体是一架顶方便的工具，我并不建议你在它之外待太久。然而，就像地球的大气把你的科学家挡在宇宙的情况之外，身体的情况也同样叫你对真正的色彩与图案设计视而不见。现在，你可以朝这个方向发展。", "en": "You have never seen what design is until you see a spider’s web when you are out of the body. You have never seen what design is until you see a spider’s web from the spider’s viewpoint. Now you can learn to do this. You can use your psychic abilities, to throw your consciousness into the spider. Your body is a very handy mechanism and I do not suggest that you step out of it too long. However, as the earth’s atmosphere hides the conditions in the universe from your scientists, so also do the conditions of the body blind you to true color and design. Now you can develop in this way.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第501节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "501", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0067", "zh": "内在感官是为感知非实质资料而准备的，它们不被你投射入三次元实相的影像所欺骗。其实，它们也能感知实质的物体。你的肉体感官是这些内在感知方法的延伸，在死后你就得依赖它们了。你在“出体”的经验中用到了它们。它们继续不断的在醒时的意识之下运作。", "en": "The inner senses are equipped to perceive data that is not physical. They are not deceived by the images that you project in three-dimensional reality. Now, they can perceive physical objects. Your physical senses are extensions of these inner methods of perception, and after death it is upon these that you will rely. They are used in out-of-body experiences. They operate constantly beneath normal waking consciousness…", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第539节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "539", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0121", "zh": "现在：在某些场合，有时在濒临死亡时，但常常只在有意识的出体情况，人可以感知那种光。举例来说，在有些出体经验里，鲁柏看见比任何实质的颜色更为眩目的颜色，而你在梦里看到同类的颜色。它们是你内在感官所感知的较大光谱的一部分，而在梦境中你根本不依赖你的肉体感官。", "en": "Now: On certain occasions, sometimes near the point of death, but often simply in conscious states outside of the body, man is able to perceive that kind of light. In some out-of-body experiences Ruburt, for example, saw colors more dazzling than any physical ones, and you saw the same kind of colors in your dream. They are a part of your inner senses’ larger spectrum of perception, and in the dream state you were not relying upon your physical senses at all.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第900节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "900", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0041", "zh": "这很难诉诸语言。同样，你们没有理由达不成出体的纯熟；等你们做到了，就能试验思想创造物——去尝试、去成形、去运用或舍弃思想绘画。在出体状态里，你们能够相当轻易地抵达那些环境：思想在那里几乎瞬间就变成了某种可塑的类物质。", "en": "This is difficult to put into words. There is no reason, again, why you can’t achieve out-of-body proficiency, and when you do, you will be able to experiment with thought creations, trying out, forming, using or discarding, thought paintings. In an out-of-body state you can reach rather easily those environments which thoughts become a sort of plastic pseudo material, almost instantaneously.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第497节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "497", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0042", "zh": "就你们特定的用途而言，你们不妨想象自己正走过、或穿行于你们自己的一幅画作之中。试着把你们的意识投进你们所画的环境里。特别去观察那些色彩——在许多出体状态中你们都看得到它们。那里有你们不曾熟悉的层次渐变。它们会激发你们自己调色板的变化。", "en": "For your particular purposes you might imagine that you are walking through, or traveling through, one of your own paintings. Try to throw your consciousness into the environment you have painted. Observe particularly the colors that would be observable to you in many out-of-body states. There are gradations with which you are not familiar. They will inspire changes in your own palette.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第497节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "497", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0043", "zh": "那里还有形形色色不同的空间关系等你们探索，然后——如果你们愿意——再设法在作品里重现它们。这些意识改变所涉及的修习，会在一切其他方面帮助你们，会让你们极为切身地结识其他实相，并为你们终将不再有可供操运的物质身体的那段时期预作准备。此处能获得一种个人证据，别无他法可以取得。鲁柏谈过要重新开展一些创作，我由衷建议你们全力专注，一同进行出体探索。", "en": "There will be all kinds of different spatial relationships for you to explore, and then to attempt to reproduce in your work if you prefer. The disciplines involved in these alterations of consciousness will help you in all other areas, will acquaint you quite personally with other realities, and be a preparation for the time when you will not have a physical body in which to manipulate. There is personal evidence to be obtained here that can be obtained in no other way. Ruburt has talked of some renewed work, and Heartily suggest that you concentrate strongly at doing joint out-of-body explorations.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第497节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "497", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "它带来的，是一份别无他法可取的个人证据", "note": "赛斯要他们练这个，要的是第一手的东西。他说当你有出体经验时，你可能开始更加直接地觉知内在实相的本质；你自己贯彻到底的出体体验甚至会反过来强化这些课，因为你要亲历的正是他已经告诉过你们的那些情形，于是你会开始问那些他视为理所当然的问题。他也承认自我对多面向的存在毫无觉知，但自我是可以教的——给它适当的资料，它某种程度还是能够了解无法直接体验的东西，所以读到别人写的关于梦与出体经验的研究，没理由感到惊讶。他还给了一个量的估算：那股支持和推动的能量若以同样的强度聚焦在一次投射上，结果就有可能达到不证自明而没有怀疑、同时被人毫无保留地接受。分寸也讲清楚了：大半宣称在精神分裂情况里发生的心电感应或千里眼，其实是个人在向自己证明全能或力量唾手可得，用来补偿平时基本的无力感；不过在某些情况里，确实有明确而真实的心电感应、千里眼的例子，有栩栩如生的出体经验，以及超出公认的实相领域的遨游。", "src": "第 259、293、304、497、921 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 259 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 293 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 304 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 497 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 921 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0020", "zh": "当你有出体经验时，你可能开始更加直接觉知内在实相的本质。", "en": "When you have out-of-body experiences, you can become aware of the nature of inner reality more directly.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第304节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "304", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0045", "zh": "你们对自己作品的信心极为重要。你们自身的出体体验若能贯彻到底，甚至会反过来强化这些课，因为你们将亲历我已经告诉过你们的那些情形。因此，你们会想到一些问题——也就是那些我视为理所当然的事。这一点你们跟上了吗？", "en": "Your faith in your own work is highly important. Your own out-of-body experiences, if followed through, will even reinforce the sessions, for you will be experiencing circumstances of which I have already told you. You will think of questions, therefore, matters that I take for granted. Do you follow me here?", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第497节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "497", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0007", "zh": "你存在很多维度中，然而自我对这样的存在毫无觉知。不过，自我是可以教的。如果给它适当的资料，它某种程度还是能够了解无法直接体验的东西。对福克斯先生那篇梦和出体经验的论文，鲁柏没有理由感到惊讶。", "en": "You exist in many dimensions, although the ego is not aware of such existence. The ego can be taught however. What it cannot experience directly it can still understand to some degree if it is given the proper information. There is no reason for Ruburt to be surprised at Mr. Fox’s thesis on dreams and out-of-body experiences.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第259节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "259", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0017", "zh": "能量，这股支持和推动的能量，用在投射上，将产生令人惊叹的结果。昨天，鲁柏的意象其实非常强烈地铭印在他班上每一个孩子的心智里。同样的能量强度用在投射上，结果就有可能不证自明而没有怀疑，同时被人接受而毫无保留。", "en": "The energy, that propelling supportive energy, used in out-of-body projections, will give astounding results. Ruburt’s image is indeed imprinted most strongly in the mind of every child in his classes yesterday, and this focused energy made this possible. Used in a projection, the same intensity of energy would allow results that could be proven without doubt, and accepted without reservation.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第293节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "293", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0124", "zh": "反之，大半宣称在精神分裂症的情况里发生的心电感应或千里眼的例子，是个人试图证明给他自己看，全能或力量之理想化的特质的确是唾手可得的——当然，这是为了补偿在较普通的作为里基本的无力感。不过，在某些情况里，有明确而十分真实的心电感应或千里眼的例子，栩栩如生的出体经验，及其他超越公认的实相领域的遨游。", "en": "Most of the declared instances of telepathy or clairvoyance that happen in schizophrenic situations are instead the individual’s attempts to prove to himself or herself that the idealized qualities of omnipotence or power are indeed within grasp—this, of course, to compensate for the basic feeling of powerlessness in more ordinary endeavors. In some situations, however, there are definite, quite valid instances of telepathy or clairvoyance, vivid out-of-body experiences, and other excursions beyond the officially accepted realm of reality.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第921节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "921", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B11", "title": "为什么这种能力在你们这里长不出来", "note": "赛斯把练不成的账有一部分算在文化头上：西方人选择了把精力向外贯注，大大忽略内心世界，社会与文化各方面、甚至连宗教方面自童年起都自动抵制这种经验——在你们的社会，会出体完全没有任何社会利益，倒有许多反对它的禁忌。科学那一头也还没开门：这些领域几乎没有做过什么科学的调查研究，最近的梦境试验非常肤浅，而在出体经验的正当性获得认可之前，根本不会做任何调查试验。他倒是给了一个可测量的线索：牵涉一些梦的因素时，梦境中的出体经验会让体温降低而不是升高。至于那些吓人的撞鬼桥段，他说你在生活之中本来就和所谓的鬼魂与幽灵同住，就此点而言你自己对其他人看来也像幽灵，特别是当你在睡眠状态放出强烈的形相，或甚至无意识地游出体外时。他也举了一个别的样子：集体做梦曾被理所当然地当成自然的人类特征，一个部落逢着荒旱在找新地点时，成员各自做梦、各管自己能力最适合的那一面，在种种方向出体旅行去看干旱的程度，回来确定迁徙的最佳方向。最后他留下一句给普通人的判断：你们可能相信眼通式的梦、出体经验、艺术上的创造性冒险都很可能，却怀疑同一股力量能不能有效地导向身体健康的实质领域或严酷的现实——而他说这份资料对实相运作方式的解释，确实比老的官方信念远较有效。", "src": "第 420、540、583、933、9 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 420 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 540 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 583 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 933 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 9 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0077", "zh": "现在来回答你的问题：西方人选择了他的精力向外贯注，而大大忽略了内心世界。社会与文化各方面，甚至连宗教方面自童年起都自动抵制了这种经验。在你们的社会，会“出体”完全没有任何社会利益，倒有许多反对它的禁忌。", "en": "Now in answer to your questions: Western man has chosen to focus his energy outward and largely ignore inner realities. The social and cultural aspects, and even the religious ones, automatically inhibit such experiences from childhood on. There is no social benefit at all connected with projections in your society, and many taboos against it.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第583节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "583", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0027", "zh": "这些领域几乎没有做过什么科学的调查研究，最近在这方面的梦境试验非常肤浅。在出体经验的正当性获得认可之前，当然就不会做任何调查试验。", "en": "Little scientific investigative work has been done in these areas. The recent dream experiments are highly superficial in this regard. Until the legitimacy of out of body experiences is recognized, no investigative experiments will be carried on, of course.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第420节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "420", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0026", "zh": "然而，梦境中的出体经验，即使牵涉到一些梦的因素，也会让体温降低，而不是升高。", "en": "In out-of-body experiences from the dream state however, there is a lowering rather than a heightening of body temperature, even though dream elements are involved.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第420节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "420", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0068", "zh": "同样地，在生活中，你就与所谓的鬼魂与幽灵同住，并且就此点而言，对其他人来说你自己也看来像是幽灵，特别是当你在睡眠状态中放出你自己强烈的“心念形相”时，或甚至当你无意识地游出体外时。", "en": "In the same way in the midst of life, you dwell with so-called ghosts and apparitions, and for that matter you yourselves appear as apparitions to others, particularly when you send strong thought-forms of yourself from the sleep state, or even when unconsciously you travel out of your physical body.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第540节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "540", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0125", "zh": "在一个时候，集体做梦是被理所当然的当成一个自然的人类特征——举例来说，在一个部落里，当逢荒旱而在找寻新的地点时，每位部落成员都会做梦，在其中那问题被加以考虑，而每位梦者处理最适合他能力及个人意向那方面的问题。梦者会在种种方向出体旅行，去看干旱的程度，并确定在任何必要的迁徙里的部落所能采取的最佳方向。", "en": "Group dreaming was at one time taken for granted as a natural human characteristic—in a tribe, for example, when new locations were being sought, perhaps in time of drought. The various tribal members would have dreams in which the problem was considered, each dreamer tackling whatever aspect of the problem that best suited his or her abilities and personal intents. The dreamers would travel out-of-body in various directions to see the extent of drought conditions, and to ascertain the best direction for the tribe to take in any needed migration.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第933节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "933", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0129", "zh": "你俩都相信，有眼通式的梦、出体经验、在艺术上的创造性冒险，是十分可能的——但到某程度，你俩却都怀疑，同样的力量或能量能被有效地导向所谓身体健康的实质领域，或严酷的现实（带着很强的幽默），再次的，对实相的运作方式，这数据的确比老的官方信念有远较有效的解释——而再次的，我们并不只在处理能唤起人的、创造性的假说而已。", "en": "You both believed it was quite possible to have clairvoyant dreams, out-of-body experiences, creative adventures in the arts — but to some extent both of you doubted that the same power or energy could be directed effectively in the physical realm, so-called, of bodily health, or situations of the nitty-gritty (with emphatic amusement). Again, the material is indeed dealing with a far more valid explanation for the working ways of reality than the old official beliefs — and again, we are not just (underlined) dealing with evocative, creative hypotheses.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第9节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "9", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [{"id": "q-concept-074-e0006", "zh": "这是一个次要建构。然而，如果垂死的哥哥在死亡之前或之后，为了探望而进行一次出体之旅，那么接收者仍然必须自己建构幻影以便感知它。但是，在这种情况下，我们就会有一个主要建构。", "en": "This would be a secondary construction. If however the dying brother made an out-of-body journey before or after death, for a last visit, then the receiver would still have to construct the apparition himself in order to perceive it. But in this case we would have a primary construction.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第253节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "253", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0009", "zh": "然后，你可以延长这个经验，视之为有效的出体之旅。意识的流动会自动赋予你更大的自由，而容许你在醒时生活中使用你的内在感知。因为这是一种意识的运动，一种和身体的运动几乎没有关系的运动。", "en": "Then you can prolong the experience, and recognize it as a valid out-of body excursion. The mobility of consciousness will automatically allow you greater freedom in using your inner perceptions in waking life also. For this is a motion of consciousness, a motion that has little to do with the motion of the physical body.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第261节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "261", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0013", "zh": "投射，出体经验，是一种创造行为，而且再一次，所有的创造行为基本上都具有攻击性。现在，你改变你的投射所在的维度。你不可能去过那些维度而不留下痕迹。", "en": "A projection, an out-of-body experience, is a creative act, and again all creative acts are basically aggressive. Now, you change those dimensions in which your projections take place. You cannot visit them and leave no mark.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第279节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "279", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0021", "zh": "我告诉过你，我们课有一些部分涉及投射。程度因课的不同而有别。有时候鲁柏将会在课间投射出体，也会记得我透过他的身体讲话时发生的事情。现在发生投射时，他在意识上对它们毫无觉知。你知道，这些事情并不是被迫的。可以说，在我们见面的其他场合，我可能很快就会讲到这一点，因为这里有相似之处和意义，牵涉到鲁柏和我自己双方使用的意识状态，以及实现的投射类型。这些与资料的清晰度或是没有扭曲的本质有关联。你看，令人不太满意的投射会导致扭曲，这是当时这种意识状态的特征。", "en": "I have told you that some portion of our sessions involves projection. The degree varies from session to session. There will be a time when Ruburt will project out of his body during sessions and remember what transpires while I speak through his body. When projections occur now he is not consciously aware of them. These things are not forced, you see. On other occasions we meet, so to speak. I will go into this perhaps soon, for there are the similarities here and significances, involving states of consciousness used by both Ruburt and myself, and the type of projection achieved. These have bearing on the clearness or undistorted nature of the material. Less satisfactory projections cause distortions, you see, that are characteristic features of this state of consciousness at that time.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第326节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "326", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0033", "zh": "我会在课上给你，或在你要求的任何时候给你。顺带说一句，等你准备好了，我在出体经验方面帮助你会相对容易。", "en": "I will give it to you in session, or at any time you request. It will be relatively easy for me to help you in out-of-body experiences, incidentally, when you are ready.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第461节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "461", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0037", "zh": "这些药物就像时间胶囊，在若干时段内削减刺激，待抵达目的定点时再注入兴奋剂。整个过程极为繁复。针剂注入肉身存有，因而作用于肉脑。意识在出体经验中投射出去。肉脑得到缓冲，以免遭受冲击——因为在这种情况下，意识行进的速度极快，正常情况下它与身体之间的联系本会被切断。", "en": "Now they are like time capsules, cutting down stimuli for certain intervals, and then injecting stimulants as destination points are reached. The process is highly involved. The injections are made into the physical being, affecting therefore the physical brain. Consciousness projects in an out of body experience. The physical brain is cushioned against shock because in this case consciousness travels at such a fast pace that ordinarily contact between it and the body would be severed.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第487节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "487", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0046", "zh": "你们功课做得越多，我就越能帮到你们。你们自己的出体功课会出现季节性以及其他方面的起伏；不过以年为单位来看，这类起伏终将熨平。在我们沟通的两端——你们那一边与我这一边——都有许多因素在帮助或阻碍着我们。", "en": "The more work you do the better I can help you. There will be seasonal and other variations in your own out-of-body work. Over a period of years however this sort of thing will iron out. There are many factors that operate to help or impede our communications, on both your side and mine.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第497节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "497", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0048", "zh": "现在。这份资料本身将在你们的协助下沿几条线推进。出体经验将是你们主观训练的一部分。我在课上对这些经验的评述，将以它们自己的方式累积起来。", "en": "Now. The material itself will progress, with your assistance, along several lines. The out-of-body experiences will be a portion of your subjective training. My comments in sessions about these experiences will add up in their own manner.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第500节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "500", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0053", "zh": "你确实已经容许自己去与你的朋友苏[Sue]会面，并在出体的状态下在那套公寓里活动。你与鲁柏之间私人、身体和心灵关系上的好转，本是你们二人这一同出体的搭档关系的必要条件。", "en": "You have indeed allowed yourself to meet with your friend Sue, and to operate within the apartment in a projected state. The change for the better in your personal, physical and psychic relationship with Ruburt was a necessity for your joint out of body partnership.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第503节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "503", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0070", "zh": "这些点叫作“交会点”，在那儿一个伪装系统并入另一个。有一些“交会点”在你们的系统里有地理上的位置，但在所有的情形里，要进入“交会点”，必要的起步就是得“调准频率”，而这种进入只能在“出体”的情况中做到。每一个人在他的梦中对“说法者”所拥有的资料都能通达。在睡眠模式里发生的与正常意识邻接的意识状态，无法被你们的EEG收到——那个邻接的“走道”，你的意识经由那儿旅行。", "en": "These are called coordination points, where one camouflage merges into the other. Some of these are geographical in your system, but in all cases, a tuning-in of consciousness is a necessary preliminary. Such entries can only be made in an out-of-body condition. Each individual in his dreams has access to the information possessed by the Speakers. There are adjacent states of consciousness that occur within the sleep pattern, that cannot be picked up by your EEG’s — adjacent “corridors” through which your consciousness travels.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第569节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "569", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0074", "zh": "在较早的一章里我已提到一些。作为珍，她大半的训练在梦境里发生。她常在“出体”的情形里去上课，最初是由各种不同的“说法者”来教导。所获的情报常经由诗而被带到有意识的层面。", "en": "I mentioned some of that in an earlier chapter. Much of her training, as Jane, took place in the dream state. There were frequent out-of-body projections in which she attended classes, taught initially by various Speakers. The information gained was often brought to conscious layers through the poetry. (Long pause at 11:15.)", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第578节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "578", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0078", "zh": "很难理解这件事，即使是我也难以解开这谜……坟墓是空的，因为这同样的团体将尸体运走了。不过，玛利亚·玛达莲娜的确在事后立刻看到了基督（见马太福音第二十八章。停顿很久）。基督是个伟大的通灵者。他于是使伤口出现在他自己身上，而且同时以肉体以及在“出体”状态出现在他的门徒前。不过，他曾试着解释所发生的事以及他所处的地位，但那些未参与阴谋者不能了解，而误解了他的声明。", "en": "(Pause at 10:00.) This is difficult to explain, and even for me to unravel…. The tomb was empty because this same group carted the body away. Mary Magdalene did see Christ, however, immediately after (see Matthew 28). (Long pause.) Christ was a great psychic. He caused the wounds to appear then upon his own body, and appeared both physically and in out-of-body states to his followers. He tried, however, to explain what had happened, and his position, but those who were not in on the conspiracy would not understand, and misread his statements.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第591节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "591", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0079", "zh": "这全被误解了。于是基督改变了他的行为方式，常常在“出体”的情况下显现给他的门徒（见约翰福音第二十、二十一章，马太福音第二十八章，路加福音第二十四章）以前他较少这样做。无论如何他是在试着告诉他们他并没有死，而他们选择当他是象征性地这样说。（停顿一分钟。）", "en": "This was all misunderstood. Christ then changed his mode of behavior, appearing quite often in out-of-body states to his followers. (See John 20, 21; Matthew 28; Luke 24.) Before, he had not done this to that degree. He tried to tell them however that he was not dead, and they chose to take him symbolically. (A one-minute pause.)", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第591节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "591", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0085", "zh": "下一章我会对这些情形略加详细的描述，至于目前，你们只要了解：在意识由外转到内时，它的确会经过一些明确的步骤与变化，而这些变化都是其来有自（其来有自：指事情的发生、发展有其来由，并非偶然。），并非毫无理由就可以的。也就是说，意识大致上先要循着一条既定的路线出发，才能朝向它所要到达的各种目的地。在人的一生中，说法者一直都在教导做梦的人，在其他境界中该怎么做，也一直在教人如何将有用的资料带回人间，以改善现世的自我。随着个人的习性、当时目标、及境界的不同，每个人对自己出体旅行这件事都有不同程度的了解。有些人很可能会对这种旅行有很深刻的印象，但是经历的本身，却常常会因大脑意识的障碍而遭到曲解。", "en": "In our next chapter I will speak of these in some detail. For now it is sufficient to realize that specific steps, definite alterations, occur as consciousness is shifted from the exterior to the interior reality, and that these changes are not random; that consciousness leaves through a very predictable route to its many destinations. Through the ages the Speakers have taught dreamers how to manipulate in these other environments. They have taught them how to bring back information that could be used for the good of the present personality. According to the intent, present purpose, and development, an individual may be aware of these travels to varying degrees. Some have excellent recall, for example, but often misinterpret their experience because of conscious ideas.", "source": "时空之外 · 第569节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "569", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-074-e0093", "zh": "没有。你的尝试开始于她上床之前，但是那些尝试都没有成功，直到她来了你才真正出体。人对时间的感觉在出体时与在肉体中时大不相同。你知道在第一次试验成功之后你才会比较自在，所以你选择了最佳的环境与时机。", "en": "No. You began your attempts before, but did not succeed until Ruburt came to bed. The time sense outside the body can be quite different than the body’s. You knew that with one successful experience you would be much more free, and so you chose the best of circumstances.", "source": "时空之外 · 第583节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "583", "only_en": false}], "books": [{"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 20}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 18}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 9}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 7}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 4}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 3}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 2}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 1}], "span": [1967, 1980], "stats": {"blocks": 11, "quotes": 73, "reading": 15, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 2}};
